a23d-57b5-97cb-eb3b71418a43" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422995 1068 #edb/ref 17592186422994 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422995 1069 "q-181950" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422995 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422995 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=N\\times \\{0,1\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422995 1072 #uuid "23754441-6057-5c56-9776-c2c2565523ab" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422995 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=N\\times \\{0,1\\}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is either $0$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in N,\\,y\\in \\{0,1\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any natural number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $0.$ \n\n$$\n{S}_{0}=\\{(x,0)\\,:\\,x\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/17/174a8dde6f409fe9f4f0aa3ea204c3b438a35b1bae607ebe2b101139fb807b99.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any natural number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$ \n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a0/a075d3109fdbd861c1e3e3103095f88691d10bcebb5708989640ca9e0a1c8931.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $N\\times \\{0,1\\}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/9c/9c3083a4394093f53ff23f74f8b37e29d20da7cb693b2755fedfbe085b0ecf11.png)" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422996 1068 #edb/ref 17592186422993 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422996 1069 "q-184491" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422996 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422996 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=(-2,0)\\times \\{2,3\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422996 1072 #uuid "a41c896d-9cc9-5fb8-affb-f5f58052d984" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true] [17592186422996 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=(-2,0)\\times \\{2,3\\}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(-2,0)$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $2$ or $3.$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in (-2,0),\\,y\\in \\{2,3\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(-2,0)$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $2$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,2)\\,:\\,x\\in (-2,0)\\}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3ff59491671c85c444afefb827c5b7cc30d617547e88f8c87b0b7edb07c5ce90.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $(-2,0)$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $3$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(x,3)\\,:\\,x\\in (-2,0)\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/45/45f703cae4149be4cc973c0537a7bb4c5fcd06b5bf3e1989004d762839154112.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the two line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/b5/b501bc9b634b38c5b0f77fc7cd4e846208076014a83029428786e36488839999.png)" 13194139534489 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0731ad6f-9b74-53f7-a4c5-a2106910f021" 17592186422983 "answer-13c030cd-fe38-5f66-8922-566fca4fcde0" 17592186422984 "answer-3b07f316-3400-5fca-be0c-a1e7f093a73d" 17592186422985 "answer-53b5a60e-4c57-51d0-914b-9ff41e97551a" 17592186422986 "answer-81bb585f-24ed-5c34-b873-a3cdcb72f6bd" 17592186422987 "answer-9af06c9a-091f-52e9-89cf-99c64bd8c45d" 17592186422988 "answer-a5187c3c-e5eb-5a68-9f79-badc55003b58" 17592186422989 "answer-d2d51c63-e17f-5acf-ac3e-0a623f345393" 17592186422990 "answer-e8c46d81-b077-54ff-ae98-d63acec7e2c0" 17592186422991 "answer-ebfdceb0-8a07-5960-9258-ee8181d936d4" 17592186422992 "answer-field-4fcce61b-be54-56a1-a84a-9e41ded26daa" 17592186422993 "answer-field-64c8a51b-a23d-57b5-97cb-eb3b71418a43" 17592186422994 "question-23754441-6057-5c56-9776-c2c2565523ab" 17592186422995 "question-a41c896d-9cc9-5fb8-affb-f5f58052d984" 17592186422996}}
